LC4 #924 — wire merge-conflict recovery into the dev-builder loop

Original task: the LC4 dev-builder loop opened PRs but never consulted the
LC7 drift-detector before merging, so a hard hunk overlap with a parallel
dev branch (or a commit landed on main since the branch was cut) could
not trigger automatic recovery in production.

Rebase note: the upstream main already shipped task #915, which added a
DIFFERENT `merge-conflict-recovery.ts` exporting `formatMergeConflictReason`,
`requestMergeConflictReplan`, and an RPC-dispatching
`createMergeConflictRecoveryHandler` (calls `system.request_dev_replan`
directly from the merge-step `onBlocked` seam). Resolution kept BOTH
feature sets per the conflict philosophy:

  - Retained #915's API verbatim: standalone-merge callers (the smoke
    script) keep `createMergeConflictRecoveryHandler` with the same
    signature + behavior.
  - Renamed our task #924 audit-only handler to
    `createMergeConflictAuditHandler` to avoid name collision.
  - `createMergeConflictPreMergeCheck` defaults its `onBlocked` to the
    audit handler so the loop's own `requestReplan` callback remains the
    sole `request_dev_replan` dispatcher (otherwise we would double-fire
    when the loop converts `drift_conflict` to verifier-red).

Changes:
- `supabase/functions/_shared/execution/builders/merge-conflict-recovery.ts`
  - #915: `formatMergeConflictReason`, `requestMergeConflictReplan`,
    `createMergeConflictRecoveryHandler` (RPC dispatcher,
    swallows + reports failures via `onReplanFailed`).
  - #924: `createMergeConflictAuditHandler` (audit-only payload write),
    `defaultComputeCurrentChanges` (whole-file conservative ranges),
    `createMergeConflictPreMergeCheck` (delegates to `runDevBuilderMerge`,
    returns `drift_conflict` on hard overlap).
- `dev-builder-runtime.ts`: `merge: { fetchOthers, computeCurrentChanges? }`
  option on `RunDevBuilderForPlanOptions`. When supplied (and no explicit
  `preMergeCheck`), the runtime composes the recovery wiring automatically.
- `supabase/functions/dev-builder/index.ts`: wires `createGithubFetchOthers`
  (24h branch-cut window) into the `merge` config so production gets the
  recovery path by default.
- `src/__tests__/lc4-merge-conflict-recovery.test.ts` (20 tests, combined):
  - #915: `formatMergeConflictReason` purity, `requestMergeConflictReplan`
    RPC behavior + error paths, recovery handler dispatches replan exactly
    once / forwards failures via `onReplanFailed`.
  - #924: audit handler appends row payload + never throws,
    `defaultComputeCurrentChanges` aggregation, pre-merge check verdicts,
    and end-to-end `runDevBuilderForPlan` recovery → rev-2 plan opens PR
    without operator intervention.

Verification: 62/62 tests pass across `lc4-merge-conflict-recovery`,
